<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mollwitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1741</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-silesian-war">First Silesian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Mollwitz was fought on 10 April 1741 in Silesia, the first major battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-silesian-war">First Silesian War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>'s army defeated the Austrians under Wilhelm Reinhard von Neipperg, although Frederick himself left the field when the battle seemed lost and Field Marshal Schwerin's infantry won it. The victory secured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>'s hold on Silesia and drew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and others into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a>.</p></div>
